<title>USA: U.S. Gulf rigs unchanged at 170 in the week.</title>
<headline>U.S. Gulf rigs unchanged at 170 in the week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>There were 170 rigs under contract in the U.S. Gulf as of June 13, unchanged from the period ending June 6, Offshore Data Services said Friday.</p>
<p>The utilization rate for rigs working in the Gulf, based on a total fleet of 178, was up 0.5 percent at 95.5 percent.</p>
<p>The number of working rigs in the European/Mediterranean area was up one at 113 rigs under contract out of a total fleet of 110, a utilization rate unchanged at 97.3 pct.</p>
<p>The worldwide rig count was down one at 577 out of a total fleet of 605, with a utilization rate of 95.4 percent, up from 95.5 percent.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk 212-859-1620</p>
</text>
